{"h":3106,"w":2400,"lines":[{"y":0.069581617215334068,"h":0.019266998084682907,"w":0.11476341247558594,"c":1,"x":0.11649047409022506,"t":"Audioscripts"},{"t":"RUSS:","y":0.12063953490814161,"c":1,"x":0.11466165384544125,"w":0.043233083089192714,"h":0.013081395234588844},{"y":0.11851514079428771,"c":1,"x":0.17832635116337278,"w":0.064399929046630833,"t":"Uh-huh.","h":0.015876695101136762},{"t":"TUTOR: I must say the handouts you prepared were well thought out. They were a good","y":0.13190426363817531,"w":0.6675691223144532,"h":0.022398426082927969,"x":0.11454232496199694,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.018996428460823056,"x":0.17669173532157495,"y":0.14970930233472779,"t":"summary of your presentation, which people would be able to refer to later on. So","w":0.61654134114583337},{"t":"well done on that.","w":0.13721804300944013,"c":1,"y":0.16709594335001698,"x":0.17669173030078056,"h":0.016097875080489321},{"y":0.18354817362355669,"w":0.088900553385416636,"c":1,"x":0.17640748706058579,"h":0.015523131248341482,"t":"Thank you."},{"t":"Well, I hope that helps you with next week's presentation.","x":0.16729322438251401,"w":0.44548873901367181,"y":0.19896973569117127,"h":0.017707662588538398,"c":1},{"h":0.011627907148116789,"y":0.21656976732557442,"t":"RUSS:","c":1,"x":0.11466165384024735,"w":0.043233083089192714},{"w":0.18421052296956383,"h":0.01458355141545753,"t":"Yes, it will. Thanks a lot.","x":0.17481203165530515,"c":1,"y":0.21506761116765549},{"t":"TUTOR: I'll look forward to seeing a big improvement, then.","c":1,"y":0.22955569880461624,"w":0.44548873901367181,"h":0.017537324565192303,"x":0.11278194641891602},{"x":0.11466165625279326,"w":0.14849623362223305,"h":0.018895348808647183,"c":1,"t":"SECTION 4","y":0.27906976726718802},{"y":0.31101094675250485,"h":0.017477425466563279,"w":0.66353383382161457,"c":1,"x":0.1146616544237791,"t":"Today, we'll be continuing the series of lectures on memory by focusing on what is called"},{"c":1,"x":0.11466165329755047,"y":0.32412790675483338,"h":0.018895348808647294,"w":0.51879699707031246,"t":"episodic memory and what can happen if this is not working properly."},{"h":0.016097875080489321,"x":0.11466165091727855,"c":1,"t":"Episodic memory refers to the memory of an event or 'episode'. Episodic memories allow us","y":0.35028976153356595,"w":0.69172932942708332},{"x":0.11269399016691466,"w":0.69002065022786463,"c":1,"h":0.017360706906585754,"t":"to mentally travel back in time to an event from the past. Episodic memories include various","y":0.36600189871171684},{"t":"details about these events, for example, when an event happened and other information such","x":0.11269007850720736,"y":0.38132846612116622,"h":0.018078578646844701,"c":1,"w":0.705058848063151},{"x":0.11267136933585391,"y":0.3963519199108243,"t":"as the location. To help understand this concept, try to remember the last time you ate dinner","w":0.69948170979817714,"h":0.02001031383114027,"c":1},{"y":0.41306956597400979,"x":0.11266529290000193,"c":1,"t":"at a restaurant. The ability to remember where you ate, who you were with and the items you","w":0.69947011311848961,"h":0.019391318405357572},{"c":1,"x":0.11260380403777456,"y":0.42789936972935605,"t":"ordered are all features of an episodic memory.","w":0.35756991068522137,"h":0.018497366945127824},{"w":0.67502670288085942,"t":"Episodic memory is distinct from another type of memory called semantic memory. This is","h":0.019589424747386008,"c":1,"x":0.11267459841678364,"y":0.45169247540445101},{"w":0.70320526123046878,"t":"the type of factual memory that we have in common with everyone else - that is your general","y":0.46902826401507902,"h":0.018356820037114807,"c":1,"x":0.1108091297937788},{"y":0.48455458257649398,"x":0.11079330361023371,"c":1,"t":"knowledge of the world. To build upon a previous example, remembering where you parked","w":0.68816314697265635,"h":0.019525492337159944},{"h":0.018353110348418356,"c":1,"x":0.1108165214025874,"t":"your car is an example of episodic memory, but your understanding of what a car is and","y":0.50059958084367429,"w":0.65994110107421877},{"h":0.018462445762029933,"c":1,"y":0.51618443265797798,"t":"how an engine works are examples of semantic memory. Unlike episodic memory, semantic","x":0.11080959016666309,"w":0.69568491617838535},{"c":1,"x":0.11266776790681396,"h":0.016925616488484341,"y":0.53256848846158999,"w":0.44575841267903638,"t":"memory isn't dependent on recalling personal experiences."},{"w":0.6580753072102864,"c":1,"x":0.11269393214118414,"h":0.018324318963792052,"y":0.55584900860048614,"t":"Episodic memory can be thought of as a process with several different steps of memory"},{"y":0.57405022539502815,"h":0.0146125650989265,"t":"processing: encoding, consolidation and retrieval.","x":0.11090226051762708,"w":0.3759398396809896,"c":1},{"y":0.59562834393875785,"c":1,"h":0.01909335873929896,"t":"The initial step is called encoding. This involves the process of receiving and registering","w":0.66000152587890626,"x":0.11079651440564381},{"h":0.018951430753669785,"c":1,"t":"information, which is necessary for creating memories of information or events that you","x":0.11078424349927256,"y":0.6118061418404791,"w":0.65436070760091147},{"y":0.62936046531321066,"h":0.01455453773198867,"x":0.11090225914747681,"t":"experience. The degree to which you can successfully encode information depends on the","w":0.67857142130533865,"c":1},{"h":0.019000626961338973,"x":0.10891641956642351,"y":0.64358848078240982,"c":1,"w":0.66187077840169273,"t":"level of attention you give to an event while it's actually happening. Being distracted can"},{"t":"make effective encoding very difficult. Encoding of episodic memories is also influenced by","x":0.11083677326386038,"y":0.65967278097127557,"w":0.6824697875976562,"h":0.017781713894698514,"c":1},{"y":0.67582263731047776,"w":0.69381240844726555,"h":0.019192504637178476,"x":0.10892547600005495,"t":"how you process the event. For example, if you were introduced to someone called Charlie.","c":1},{"y":0.69202200553113302,"w":0.67866551717122403,"t":"you might make the connection that your uncle has the same name. Future recollection of","c":1,"x":0.10898072069106983,"h":0.01603445604549103},{"x":0.11079108680365346,"t":"Charlie's name is much easier if you have a strategy to help you encode it","w":0.55847249348958328,"y":0.70671936005696223,"h":0.017975797978663444,"c":1},{"x":0.11079256770042245,"y":0.73104833000471925,"t":"Memory consolidation, the next step in forming an episodic memory, is the process by which","w":0.69192240397135418,"h":0.019760792591613341,"c":1},{"h":0.014534883321060788,"w":0.67669174194335935,"c":1,"y":0.74854651182456811,"t":"memories of encoded information are strengthened, stabilised and stored to facilitate later","x":0.11090224919783187},{"t":"retrieval. Consolidation is most effective when the information being stored can be linked to","w":0.69005350748697913,"y":0.76265868610011767,"c":1,"x":0.10893350495565832,"h":0.017908613373215365},{"x":0.10893173765955699,"y":0.7788425630397019,"w":0.69943664550781248,"h":0.018568666535504597,"c":1,"t":"an existing network of information. Consolidation makes it possible for you to store memories"},{"y":0.7940712862210666,"h":0.019849499655169023,"x":0.10702760752012939,"w":0.69948842366536457,"t":"for later retrieval indefinitely. Forming strong memories depends on the frequency with which","c":1},{"x":0.10894908867018045,"y":0.81052464791156131,"w":0.68810073852539055,"h":0.01832036241284507,"t":"you try to retrieve them. Memories can fade or become harder to retrieve if they aren't used","c":1},{"t":"very often.","y":0.82689545089999572,"h":0.01616370071538864,"c":1,"x":0.10870981010408923,"w":0.083188076019287127},{"w":0.6336874389648437,"t":"The last step in forming episodic memories is called retrieval, which is the conscious","y":0.85004050293364763,"h":0.018625648729431177,"c":1,"x":0.10890523437937503},{"c":1,"x":0.10704377595689513,"h":0.018442955925935922,"w":0.6825302632649739,"y":0.86570560807623365,"t":"recollection of encoded information. Retrieving information from episodic memory depends"},{"x":0.10895951649959017,"h":0.017436226490460505,"w":0.684334208170573,"t":"upon semantic, olfactory, auditory and visual factors. These help episodic memory retrieval","c":1,"y":0.88251712691789319},{"c":1,"y":0.8975473844734162,"x":0.108937441014664,"h":0.017931103629599265,"t":"by acting as a prompt. For example, when recalling where you parked your car you may use","w":0.69189615885416667},{"h":0.018536280910199654,"c":1,"y":0.91374416451196627,"x":0.10705668176343494,"t":"the colour of a sign close to where you parked. You actually have to mentally travel back to","w":0.68438206990559891},{"c":1,"t":"the moment you parked","w":0.18079517364501951,"h":0.016827345662015714,"y":0.93013584988655229,"x":0.10882501073302407},{"w":0.035714286168416334,"t":"106","y":0.96947674424063235,"x":0.10902255629549108,"c":1,"h":0.014534883321060788},{"h":0.018895348808647294,"x":0.82706766986817093,"t":"Q30","y":0.13372093008937791,"w":0.039473683039347396,"c":1},{"w":0.03803898175557463,"c":1,"t":"Q31","h":0.016068564793868645,"x":0.82410988478690073,"y":0.36702085010429863},{"x":0.82518796920296289,"y":0.45639534885585875,"h":0.013081395234588844,"w":0.033834587732950783,"c":1,"t":"Q32"},{"t":"Q34","y":0.630813953504617,"h":0.013081395234588733,"c":1,"x":0.82330827036151544,"w":0.03571428616841632},{"y":0.67877906978609137,"c":1,"x":0.82330826995484252,"h":0.013081395234588844,"w":0.033834587732950783,"t":"Q35"},{"w":0.033834587732950783,"x":0.82142857070672226,"y":0.8851744186233006,"t":"Q38","h":0.013081395234588733,"c":1}]}